{"title":"Career Roadmap · Botanist","role":"Botanist","summary":"Career objective: Build expertise in plant biology, ecology, taxonomy, plant physiology, genetics, conservation and applied plant science, progressing from a B.Sc. foundation into research, environmental science, agriculture, biotechnology, conservation or academic careers.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Botanist's work can span:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Plant Biology","Ecology","Taxonomy","Conservation","Research","Data/Technology"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc. Botany + plant biology + laboratory + fieldwork"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Research Assistant / Botanical Field Researcher / Plant Science roles"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"M.Sc. + specialised research / project positions"}],[{"text":"2037–2042"},{"text":"Scientist / Ecologist / Plant Researcher / Conservation Specialist"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Principal Scientist / Senior Researcher / Professor / Botanical Research Lead"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A B.Sc. alone can provide entry-level opportunities, but independent research and long-term scientific careers usually require an M.Sc., and often a Ph.D. for scientist, university faculty and advanced research positions."}]},{"heading":"What to build during B.Sc.","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Plant biology foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"Plant diversity"},{"text":"Plant morphology"},{"text":"Plant anatomy"},{"text":"Plant physiology"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Evolution"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Basic chemistry"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn scientific observation and documentation."