{"text":"Conservation biology"},{"text":"Climate-change impacts on plants"},{"text":"Plant-microbe interactions"},{"text":"Plant pathology"},{"text":"Plant biotechnology"},{"text":"Medicinal plants"},{"text":"Ethnobotany"},{"text":"Invasive species"},{"text":"Restoration ecology"},{"text":"Plant-pollinator interactions"},{"text":"Plant adaptation"},{"text":"Crop improvement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong future research areas"},{"type":"h","text":"Plant Genomics + Bioinformatics"},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"flow","items":["Climate Change","Plant Ecology","Remote Sensing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 career evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Traditional botany:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field Observation","Species Identification","Classification","Research"]},{"type":"p","text":"is increasingly becoming:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field Data + Genomics + GIS + Remote Sensing + AI","Ecological Modelling","Conservation Decisions"]},{"type":"p","text":"Future Botanists will increasingly use:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DNA barcoding"},{"text":"Genomics"},{"text":"Bioinformatics"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Satellite imagery"},{"text":"Drone imagery"},{"text":"AI-based species identification"},{"text":"Ecological modelling"},{"text":"Climate datasets"},{"text":"Biodiversity databases"},{"text":"Digital herbariums"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI and computer vision can assist plant identification, but expert taxonomic validation remains important, especially for difficult or closely related species."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Botany"},{"type":"flow","items":["Plant Taxonomy","Anatomy","Physiology","Genetics","Plant Diversity"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Ecology"},{"type":"flow","items":["Biodiversity","Ecology","Conservation","Climate Science"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Experimental Design","Statistics","Scientific Writing","Literature Review"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory"},{"type":"flow","items":["Microscopy","DNA Techniques","PCR","Plant Tissue Methods","Biochemical Analysis"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Field"},{"type":"flow","items":["Plant Identification","Sampling","Herbarium","Biodiversity Surveys","GPS"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"flow","items":["R/Python","Statistics","GIS","Remote Sensing","Bioinformatics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Future"},{"type":"flow","items":["Genomics","AI Species Identification","Ecological Modelling","Climate Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Botany","Field/Laboratory Internship","Research Assistant / Botanical Field Assistant","M.Sc. Botany / Plant Science / Ecology","Specialise in Taxonomy, Ecology, Physiology, Biotechnology, Conservation or Molecular Biology","Research Scientist / Botanist / Ecologist / Plant Scientist","Ph.D.","Senior Scientist / Principal Researcher / Professor"]},{"type":"note","label":"Best overall strategy","text":"treat the B.Sc. as the foundation and build a strong combination of plant biology + fieldwork + laboratory research + statistics. For a long-term professional Botanist or research career, an M.Sc. followed by a Ph.D. is usually the strongest route. Adding GIS, remote sensing, bioinformatics and AI-assisted biodiversity analysis makes the profile substantially more future-ready."},{"type":"table","header":["ID","Level","Category","Degree","Course","Target Career"],"rows":[[{"text":"706"},{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Science"},{"text":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)"},{"text":"Botany"},{"text":"Plant Pathologist"}]]}]}]}